URL:https://ece.princeton.edu/events/towards-physics-guided-wireless-commun
 ication-and-sensing-above-100-ghz-0
LOCATION:EQUAD J323
SUMMARY:Towards Physics-Guided Wireless Communication and Sensing Above 100
  GHz
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:&nbsp\;The sub-Terahertz (sub-THz) bands - frequencies above 10
 0 GHz and up to 1 THz - are rapidly emerging as one of the accepted paradi
 gms for future wireless networks. In principle\, these frequencies can pro
 vide ultra-fast data transmission due to their large amount of available b
 andwidth. Nonetheless\, several fundamental challenges stand in the way of
  their adoption. Instead of merely scaling the existing wireless system ar
 chitecture\, my thesis investigates how to leverage the physics of sub-THz
  signals to overcome these hurdles.
CATEGORIES:Final Public Oral Examinations,Final Public Orals
